.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.db
*.sqlite3
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
.DS_Store

# Evaluation output. The shards are ~320 MB and stay out. The four manifests
# are ~380 KB and ship, because README's "check the cryptography without
# trusting us" snippet opens one, and tests/test_report.py's drift guards
# skip -- silently, on a green run -- when they are absent. A judge cloning
# this repo should be able to check every published figure without a nine-hour
# regeneration. out/holdout/evaluation.json additionally cannot be
# regenerated at all: EVALUATION.md 3c allows the holdout one run, and it has
# been spent.
out/*
!out/development/
!out/holdout/
!out/adversary/
!out/shadow/
out/development/*
!out/development/evaluation.json
out/holdout/*
!out/holdout/evaluation.json
out/adversary/*
!out/adversary/redteam.json
out/shadow/*
# Both the JSON and the rendered .txt: the text table is what a reader
# actually reads, and it carries the partial-run warning inline.
!out/shadow/classifier_comparison*

# Cassettes ship. They are 164 KB, they carry no credential (provider, model,
# prompt, response_text), and without them `make shadow` fails with
# CassetteMiss on a fresh clone -- which defeats the purpose of having
# recorded them. Replay is the default everywhere, so shipping them makes the
# comparison reproducible offline and for free.
